  "query_preview": "/Sunday through Thursday/...\nCome Sunday, there is greater long-range guidance agreement on \nthe upper low merged with a Pacific longwave trough steering \nnortheast of our area over Montana. This pattern shift will \nbegin a warming and drying trend Sunday through the end of the \nextended period. Temperatures on Sunday will sit right around \nnormal, warming to 10-15 degrees above normal by Wednesday. \nLong-range projections hint at a weak and mostly dry shortwave \ntrough digging over over our area late Wednesday into Thursday. \nFor now, Thursday will most likely see dry conditions and above \nnormal temperatures.",
